%description:

Which slot of the carrier vectors a carrier occupies must not reach a result.

A component carrier is identified by its frequency -- that is what the Binder
keys its per-carrier structures on -- so two carriers cannot be identical and
"the same scenario on two identical carriers" is not a thing that can be
configured. The testable statement is the one that matters anyway: exchanging
which index holds which frequency has to exchange the two carriers' results
and change nothing else.

That is a direct exercise of the per-carrier channelModel[] vector, which is
a structure any refactoring of the medium has to rebuild, and of the
componentCarrierModule wiring that ties each channel model to its carrier. An
index leaking into the physics -- a state map keyed on the carrier's position
rather than on its frequency, say -- would show here and almost nowhere else.

The whole recorded result set is compared, with the carrier indices relabelled
in the module names. A name with no counterpart is a failure rather than a
silent skip, because a relabelling rule that quietly covers less than it
should is exactly how this kind of test stops testing anything. The one
exclusion is stated at the grader: the UE's LTE channel model has a single
carrier, so it has no index to be exchanged with.

Everything random is switched off, so what remains between the two carriers
is the frequency-dependent path loss -- 81.22 dB of SINR on the 2 GHz carrier
against 71.68 dB on the 6 GHz one -- and the two runs have to agree on which
of those belongs to which frequency rather than to which slot.

%extraargs: -c CarrierSymmetry

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config CarrierSymmetry]
output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 5s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
seed-set = 0
**.vector-recording = false
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

# Which carrier index holds which frequency. Only the frequency should reach
# a result; the index is a position in a vector.
**.swapped = ${swap = 0, 1}
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 2
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = (${swap} == 0 ? 2GHz : 6GHz)
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].carrierFrequency = (${swap} == 0 ? 6GHz : 2GHz)
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].numBands = 6

*.gnb.cellularNic.numCarriers = 2
*.gnb.cellularNic.channelModel[0].componentCarrierModule = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0]"
*.gnb.cellularNic.channelModel[1].componentCarrierModule = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"
*.ue[*].cellularNic.numNrCarriers = 2
*.ue[*].cellularNic.nrChannelModel[0].componentCarrierModule = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0]"
*.ue[*].cellularNic.nrChannelModel[1].componentCarrierModule = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"

*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.gnb.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.numUe = 1
*.ue[0].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[0].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 400m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

**.scenario = "URBAN_MACROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false
**.numBands = 6

*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 1
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 100B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.01s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=1 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
